From 9167c636c5870991e4df0f180f39c9847f353fa9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:07:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Seed a folder's blank draft in SQL, and again when its
 imported release goes

A folder this device did not import read as its blank draft when it held no draft row, so the pane and the window rebuilt it from the files on every read. The scan now stores the folder's blank cover with its files, seeds the blank draft from the stored audio units, and deleting this device's release of a folder seeds it again (a trigger, since coven applies another device's deletion too). Every such state holds a draft row, and the pane fails on a missing one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019wwAR8vet2nCM1HhYR5VRz
